  "plain": "Joe Rogan, a well-known podcast host, tells of a man named Thomas Baron who, he says, was hired by NASA, the US space agency, around 1967 to assess how likely its programme was to succeed. According to Rogan, Baron wrote a 500-page report, was then killed by a train, and the report vanished. Rogan tells it as a sign that someone may have wanted Baron's findings buried."
